WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.482
PenGPT

00:00:01.683 --> 00:00:02.944
small transformers

00:00:02.756 --> 00:00:03.628
that write in

00:00:03.593 --> 00:00:04.819
anyone's handwriting

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.878
Sam Greydanus trained

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.671
a 6M-parameter model

00:00:08.483 --> 00:00:09.520
that writes print

00:00:09.379 --> 00:00:10.546
and cursive and

00:00:10.511 --> 00:00:11.973
imitates an unseen

00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:12.598
writer from a

00:00:12.409 --> 00:00:13.352
few words

00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:15.711
plus a 54M-parameter

00:00:15.523 --> 00:00:16.595
model that draws

00:00:16.407 --> 00:00:17.173
from text

00:00:17.268 --> 00:00:18.576
using one pen-stroke

00:00:18.388 --> 00:00:19.838
tokenizer for both

00:00:20.374 --> 00:00:21.612
The handwriting data

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.291
495,590 words by

00:00:25.103 --> 00:00:27.708
1,255 writers

00:00:27.886 --> 00:00:28.723
was built from

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:29.925
scanned pages with

00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:31.234
a vision-language model

00:00:31.058 --> 00:00:32.437
and InkSight tracing

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:33.874
The author says

00:00:33.685 --> 00:00:34.534
the effort was

00:00:34.393 --> 00:00:35.501
80% data

00:00:35.655 --> 00:00:37.211
15% speed and

00:00:37.023 --> 00:00:38.579
5% architecture

00:00:38.662 --> 00:00:39.522
and that Claude

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:40.159
wrote most of

00:00:39.971 --> 00:00:40.961
the post text

00:00:41.478 --> 00:00:42.492
Full story on

00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:43.199
the dashboard
